# HOME — What openOODA is

File: guide/Home.oot
User wiki. Canonical URL: https://openooda.org/guide/#Home.oot
Pin: v0.204.0-beta.

## 1. In one minute

openOODA is a systems language. You write `.oo` files.
A systems language talks to the machine.

Effects need a capability token.
A capability token is a permission the function holds.
No token, no effect.

The product path is:

1. Typecheck the program.
2. Emit C.
3. Compile that C with host `gcc`.
4. Run the binary.

That path is `ooda run`.
More on the path: [How it works](Limits.oot).

First run: [Start](Use.oot).
Tokens: [Capabilities](Safety.oot). Fuel, path scope, and host scope are libraries on that page.
Add a package: [Packages](Packages.oot).
HTTP 402 / x402: [Pay](Pay.oot) is a library you import into an `.oo` program. A tip quote is `GET https://pay.openooda.org/tip`. The door does not charge.

The public system is three places: door, guide, store.

Door: https://openooda.org/
Guide: https://openooda.org/guide/
Store: https://registry.openooda.org

